<section class="py-24 px-6 bg-white">
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center">

    <!-- Photo placeholder -->
    <div class="fade-up mx-auto mb-8 w-24 h-24 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-blue-tint)] border-2 border-[var(--color-blue-accent)]/20 flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden">
      <svg class="w-12 h-12 text-[var(--color-blue-accent)]/40" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path d="M12 12c2.7 0 4.8-2.1 4.8-4.8S14.7 2.4 12 2.4 7.2 4.5 7.2 7.2 9.3 12 12 12zm0 2.4c-3.2 0-9.6 1.6-9.6 4.8v2.4h19.2v-2.4c0-3.2-6.4-4.8-9.6-4.8z"/>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <h2 class="fade-up delay-1 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-heading font-700 text-[var(--color-heading)] tracking-tight mb-5 text-balance">
      Built by someone who had the same problem
    </h2>

    <p class="fade-up delay-2 text-base text-[var(--color-body)] leading-relaxed">
      I started taking a handful of supplements and quickly realized I had no idea if they were safe to take together — or when to take them. Every search led to conflicting information or nothing at all. So I built StackWise to answer that question properly, with real citations and a schedule that actually fits how I live.
    </p>

    <p class="fade-up delay-3 mt-4 text-sm font-heading font-600 text-[var(--color-heading)]">
      Alfonso C. — iOS developer
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
